ork. No client diversity cap applies (bug affects all nodes receiving the malicious data via P2P). An attacker can trigger this via P2P gossip by crafting DataColumnSidecar M with valid inclusion proof (copied from a legitimate sidecar) but malicious KzgCommitments. When M arrives after a legitimate sidecar with the same proof/header, the cache hit causes M to skip verification, causing acceptance of invalid commitments and propagation to peers.",
